# Backend architecture - Spring Modulith

## Structure per module
Each domain module must follow:
- api/ (controllers, DTOs, OpenAPI surface)
- application/ (use cases, orchestration)
- domain/ (aggregates, rules, domain events)
- infrastructure/ (JPA repositories, adapters)

## Boundaries
- Cross-module calls: only via another module's api/ or via domain events.
- No direct references to domain/application packages of other modules.
- Shared kernel must be minimal and placed in a dedicated common area only when proven necessary.

## Traceability
- For each endpoint or use case, add a short comment or doc reference pointing to legacy source (Action/JSP/DAO) that it replaces.
